⍝ An event type and a kernel in Arvo's shape: a door [battery state]
⍝ (SPEC.md section 4.1).  The battery holds the arms poke, peek and
⍝ load at axes 4, 10 and 11 of the kernel; the state is axis 3.  The
⍝ runtime pulls an arm by axis and applies it to the whole kernel, as
⍝ Nock 9 does, so an arm reaches its own battery and state without
⍝ naming itself.  Nothing is reified; the runtime selects and applies.
nat ≡ Zero | Suc nat
event ≡ Tick | Poke nat
effect ≡ Log nat
effects ≡ Nil | Cons effect effects

add m n = n ▹ { Zero m; Suc k (Suc (add m k)) }

⍝ poke: kernel -> event -> [effects kernel'].  The new kernel keeps
⍝ this battery and replaces the state.
poke k ev = ev ▹ { Tick [Nil [(2⊑k) (Suc (3⊑k))]]; Poke n [(Cons (Log (3⊑k)) Nil) [(2⊑k) (add (3⊑k) n)]] }

⍝ peek: kernel -> path -> answer.  Every path reads the counter.
peek k p = 3⊑k

⍝ load: kernel -> old state -> kernel'.  This battery over the old state.
load k old = [(2⊑k) old]

kernel ≔ [[poke [peek load]] Zero]
